{"operations":[{"content":"The general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present, as amended on 2 May 2026[[cite:obs-ff113a3b1875159208e86e806097711614f91d4c \"the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present.\"]]. Where the amendment of 2 May 2026 and the bylaws differ, the amendment applies. The bylaws state that the general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present[[cite:obs-8246a9ae98ae77d9006c2b94a720237df29feaf1 \"The general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present.\"]].","expected_sha256":"436a15c7e332c0d188ca4600961246fbd84f9499c7fef4c72f7d8c338d24b363","kind":"modify","path":"doc/quorum.md"}],"rationale":"Added the quorum definition from the 2 May 2026 amendment, stated that it overrides the bylaws, and included the original bylaws quorum for completeness, with exact citations."}